1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,203
We've been looking at different types of conflicts that may arise between wildlife

2
00:00:06,203 --> 00:00:12,850
and humans at the boundaries of protected areas such as national parks and animal sanctuaries.

3
00:00:12,850 --> 00:00:24,992
I'd like to illustrate this by telling you about some research that I've been involved in recently in the central African country of Zambia in the area around the Chembe Bird Sanctuary,

4
00:00:24,992 --> 00:00:28,920
which contains over three hundred of the listed birds of Zambia.

5
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:32,330
These include a number of birds of prey,

6
00:00:32,330 --> 00:00:34,840
such as eagles, hawks and owls

7
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:39,150
that live by hunting and killing other birds and animals.

8
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:46,942
Now, most of the people living in the local communities near to the bird sanctuary are small-scale farmers,

9
00:00:46,942 --> 00:00:52,570
and these birds of prey provide important social and ecological benefits to them.

10
00:00:52,570 --> 00:00:58,334
For example, a lot of damage can be caused to farmers' crops by rodents such as rats,

11
00:00:58,334 --> 00:01:05,455
which would consume the crops as they grow in the fields as well as after harvesting if they weren't hunted

12
00:01:05,455 --> 00:01:07,150
and killed by the birds.

13
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:12,830
And the predatory habits of these birds also protect farmers in other ways.

14
00:01:12,830 --> 00:01:17,720
For example, a major danger to rural workers is snakes

15
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:20,649
whose bite may be dangerous or even fatal,

16
00:01:20,649 --> 00:01:26,730
and birds of prey have a major role in keeping their populations under control.

17
00:01:26,730 --> 00:01:31,680
Local people have always been aware of these benefits and for years,

18
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:35,240
even before the sanctuary was opened in 1973

19
00:01:35,820 --> 00:01:39,930
the birds played a key role in the culture of the region.

20
00:01:39,930 --> 00:01:42,483
However, more recently, the sanctuary

21
00:01:42,483 --> 00:01:51,162
and its birds have also become increasingly important to the community in economic terms, because at present,

22
00:01:51,162 --> 00:01:53,900
after a relatively slow start

23
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:58,820
tourism has become an important source of revenue for them.

24
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:06,070
However, although these birds of prey are protected by the government, their numbers are falling.

25
00:02:06,070 --> 00:02:08,530
Some of these deaths are accidental.

26
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:12,120
Fatalities occur when birds alight on roads to catch

27
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:16,350
and eat their prey, and are hit by fast-moving traffic.

28
00:02:16,350 --> 00:02:20,395
Drivers in Zambia have to take special care at night,

29
00:02:20,395 --> 00:02:25,250
as birds may regard the quieter roads as safe places to sleep.

30
00:02:25,250 --> 00:02:27,660
Accidental deaths may also occur

31
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:31,498
if these birds fly close to high-voltage power lines,

32
00:02:31,498 --> 00:02:33,730
as they may be electrocuted.

33
00:02:33,730 --> 00:02:37,215
This is a particular danger in the heavy rain

34
00:02:37,215 --> 00:02:42,250
which can occur in the region in the months from December to April.

35
00:02:42,250 --> 00:02:46,610
And local farmers also pose a threat to these birds.

36
00:02:46,610 --> 00:02:52,440
As well as growing crops, small-scale farmers in the area also rear chickens.

37
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:55,080
These provide food for the farmers' families

38
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:58,910
as well as being an important source of income.

39
00:02:58,910 --> 00:03:03,565
But they're also an easy target for birds of prey,

40
00:03:03,565 --> 00:03:08,643
and so farmers may shoot these birds, which is illegal but understandable,

41
00:03:08,643 --> 00:03:10,640
or they may poison the birds

42
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:16,260
which again is illegal and can have negative effects on the ecosystem.

43
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:21,820
So how else can farmers protect their chickens from birds of prey?

44
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:26,280
Some people believe that to prevent the predators from settling near the area

45
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:31,780
where the chickens are kept it's best to keep this area free from vegetation.

46
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:37,743
But in fact this is counter-productive as it means the chickens have no cover to hide in

47
00:03:37,743 --> 00:03:41,250
and they'll be easier for the birds to see.

48
00:03:41,250 --> 00:03:46,547
Another possibility would be to prevent the chickens from going outside at all,

49
00:03:46,547 --> 00:03:50,621
and to keep them safe from predators inside a building,

50
00:03:50,621 --> 00:03:55,510
but this would cost far too much to be a practical solution.

51
00:03:55,510 --> 00:04:00,213
Nearly all the farmers reported that they spent a lot of time

52
00:04:00,213 --> 00:04:05,700
and effort trying to frighten off the birds of prey without actually harming them.

53
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:08,560
Most of the farmers had at least one dog

54
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:13,370
and said this was a big help at scaring away the predators.

55
00:04:13,370 --> 00:04:17,583
Some of the farmers also reported that during the breeding season,

56
00:04:17,583 --> 00:04:19,881
when the chickens were particularly vulnerable,

57
00:04:19,881 --> 00:04:23,820
they encouraged their children to watch over the chickens

58
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:26,393
and to hit pans with a metal spoon

59
00:04:26,393 --> 00:04:33,670
so that the resulting noise would succeed in driving away birds that were trying to seize the young chicks.

60
00:04:33,670 --> 00:04:37,365
None of these methods was a hundred per cent effective,

61
00:04:37,365 --> 00:04:43,277
so as a result, the village people told us that rather than just using one method,

62
00:04:43,277 --> 00:04:48,080
they were forced to use a combination for them to have any effect.

63
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:54,946
And even so, these birds of prey remain a major threat to the chickens' survival

64
00:04:54,946 --> 00:04:58,150
and cause considerable economic loss to farmers.

65
00:04:58,150 --> 00:05:04,380
So we looked at the possibility of a longer-term solution to...
